go/types records an object for a blank name, so a //plumb directive on func _()
reaches discover; a blank identifier cannot be called, so it is rejected rather
than emitted as an unusable _() reference.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrBlankProvider
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

//plumb:build
func _() int { return 0 }
